/-!
# Extended centralizers in the perfect four-cover

The shared geometry preserves the source overgroup, normalizer coordinates,
and chosen involutions. It supplies the embedded E₉ residual and a diagonal
element of order three outside it. The full odd-core and Sylow identification
still require the residual-action calculation and its finite-group consequences.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.3.38, printed pp.1136--1137.
-/
